  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a positive integer NNN, construct two arrays AAA and BBB, each of size NNN such that:\n\n\nAi≠AjA_i \\ne A_jAi​=Aj​ for all (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i \\lt j \\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N);\nBi≠BjB_i \\ne B_jBi​=Bj​ for all (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i \\lt j \\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N);\nAi≠BjA_i \\ne B_jAi​=Bj​ for all (1≤i,j≤N)(1\\le i,j \\le N)(1≤i,j≤N);\n1≤Ai,Bi≤3⋅1051 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤Ai​,Bi​≤3⋅105 for all (1≤i≤N)(1\\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N);\n⊕A[1,i]=⊕B[1,i]\\oplus A[1,i] = \\oplus B[1,i]⊕A[1,i]=⊕B[1,i] for all (1≤i≤N)(1\\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N) such that iii is **even**.\nHere ⊕A[L,R]\\oplus A[L,R]⊕A[L,R] corresponds to the bitwise XOR of all elements of the subarray [L,R][L,R][L,R] of array AAA. Similarly, ⊕B[L,R]\\oplus B[L,R]⊕B[L,R] corresponds to the bitwise XOR of all elements of the subarray [L,R][L,R][L,R] of array BBB.\n\nIf multiple answers are possible, ouput any.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains of a single line of input, a single integer NNN - as mentioned in statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output two lines.\n\n\n\nThe first line contains NNN space-separated integers denoting the elements of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers denoting the elements of the array BBB.\n\nIf multiple answers are possible, ouput any.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤2171 \\leq N \\leq 2^{17}1≤N≤217",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤3⋅1051 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤Ai​,Bi​≤3⋅105",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2182^{18}218."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
